## Scope — read before reusing a specific part

This MIT license covers this repository's **original work**: the Claude Code skill at
`.claude/skills/openscad/` (its own scripts/templates — excluding the vendored BOSL2 library,
which carries its own BSD-2-Clause license at
`.claude/skills/openscad/templates/libraries/BOSL2/LICENSE`), the documentation, and the parts
with no third-party attribution header.

It does **not** cover the parts adapted from other creators' designs — those remain under
whatever the original creator specified, stated in that file's own header comment:

| Part | Original creator | Stated terms |
|---|---|---|
| [`customizable_U_hook_updated`](openscad-projects/customizable_U_hook_updated/src/main.scad) | Serge Payen | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (explicit in header) |
| [`Customizable_Card_Box`](openscad-projects/Customizable_Card_Box/src/main.scad) | Lufton ([thing:2404395](https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:2404395)) | Not stated in header — check the Thingiverse page before reuse |
| [`CustomizableWallPlate`](openscad-projects/CustomizableWallPlate/src/main.scad) | unattributed by name ([thing:47956](http://www.thingiverse.com/thing:47956)) | Not stated in header — check the Thingiverse page before reuse |
| [`KeyCap`](openscad-projects/KeyCap/src/main.scad) | multiple contributors (see in-file credits) | Mixed — at least one embedded component states public domain; others unstated |

"Not stated in header" means: don't assume permissive reuse. Thingiverse's default license for
designs that don't pick one explicitly is **all-rights-reserved**, not CC. Check the linked
Thingiverse page for the creator's actual license selection before redistributing or reusing
those four files specifically.
